{
  "sections" : [ {
    "type" : "Heading",
    "heading" : "Step 1: Domain Context",
    "body" : "This is a correlation scatter plot dashboard showing rating correlations by customer segment — measuring how ease of buying/using/reliability correlates with expertise, satisfaction, and recommendation ratings, segmented by gender, industry, job function, and length of being a customer.",
    "viewClientId" : "2214703224885305596",
    "children" : [ ]
  }, {
    "type" : "Heading",
    "heading" : "Step 2: Review All Data Facts",
    "body" : "All 5 outlier marks share the same measure (sum of Number of Records), all are high values, and all belong to the \"2+ Years\" customer tenure segment. Key groupings:\n- 4 of 5 are Male, Accounting industry, 2+ Years: Finance (59), Sales (45), Other (38), Marketing (36)\n- 1 is Female, Construction, Finance, 2+ Years (34)",
    "viewClientId" : "2214703224885305596",
    "children" : [ ]
  }, {
    "type" : "Heading",
    "heading" : "Step 3: Generate Insights",
    "body" : "All 5 facts reference the same measure field (Number of Records) and the same dimension value (2+ Years). They all point to the same business takeaway: the largest customer clusters in this dataset are long-tenured (2+ Year) customers, with Male/Accounting being especially dominant. These should be combined.\nHowever, there are two distinct sub-stories worth separating: (1) the Male + Accounting cluster dominance, and (2) the broader 2+ Years pattern including the Female/Construction outlier. But since they all share the same measure and same tenure dimension, I'll combine into one comprehensive insight. Given 5 facts all pointing to the same pattern, one strong insight is the right call.\n```json\n{\n\"visualizationName\": \"Correlation\",\n\"insights\": [\n{\n\"text\": \"The largest data clusters in this chart are all long-tenured customers (2+ Years), with Male respondents in the Accounting industry standing out most — the Finance job function alone accounts for 59 records, followed by Sales (45), Other (38), and Marketing (36). These are the segments driving the biggest bubbles you see on screen, and notably, they all rate the product highly across satisfaction, reliability, and recommendation — suggesting that longer customer relationships are strongly associated with better outcomes across the board.\",\n\"rank\": 1,\n\"artifactIDs\": [\"a4d506f49b16d611\", \"1250f093febbd11d\", \"408ddac71bd95517\", \"1c82bcb633bd6c16\", \"79f5e9d23d97537e\"]\n}\n]\n}\n```",
    "viewClientId" : "2214703224885305596",
    "children" : [ ]
  } ]
}

{
  "sections" : [ {
